+### Streaming Response
+
+Set `"stream": true` to receive `200 OK` with `Content-Type: text/event-stream`.
+Streaming requests run directly when the model context becomes available and do
+not create an async job or return a polling URL. Model load/unload is blocked
+while a streaming response is running. If the model changes before streaming
+starts, the response reports an SSE error.
+
+The first event reports that generation is starting:
+
+```text
+data: {"status":"starting"}
+```
+
+Sampling progress events use the same fields for image and video models:
+
+```text
+data: {"step":4,"total_steps":28,"percentage":14.29,"time_per_step":1.25,"eta":30.0,"timestamp":1775401200}
+```
+
+The completion event contains the encoded video and `generation_info` metadata.
+Audio generated by models such
+as Minimax H3 or LTX is included in the output container when the selected
+format supports audio.
+
+```text
+data: {"status":"completed","created":1775401215,"output_format":"webm","mime_type":"video/webm","fps":16,"frame_count":33,"b64_json":"GkXfo..."}
+
+data: [DONE]
+```
+
+Generation failures produce an error event followed by `[DONE]`:
+
+```text
+data: {"status":"error","error":"generate_video returned no results"}
+
+data: [DONE]
+```
+
 ### Reference Image Rules
 
 - `ref_images` contains reference images for MiniMax-H3 Ref2VA conditioning.
